    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0239" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg147"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr.
                            Hay</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Pekin, China</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1899-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                                1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 203.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report the conclusion
                    of arrangements for the extension of the Shanghai settlement, the details of
                    which have already been transmitted to the Department by Consul-General
                    Goodnow.</p>
                <p>They have my approval and I trust will be satisfactory to the Department of
                    State.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
